    "problems": [
      {
        "category": "documentation_staleness_sweep",
        "summary": "Flipping a production default invalidated statements in five separate documents, and Arch scoped the brief around only the two it had thought of. The remaining three surfaced one at a time across two reviewer rounds, each costing a correction round, until the correction allowance ran out with one annotation still unconfirmed.",
        "evidence": "Round 0 covered kpp_parameters.py, kpp_routines.py and model_contract.md. Richard's round-0 must_fix added possible_kpp_bugs_in_mitgcm.md and critical_lessons_fortran_to_python_porting.md; his round-1 must_fix added three further unannotated spots inside the first of those (lines 240, the kpp_parameters excerpt, and the Validation Impact bullet). Bob reached the scope's corrections limit of 2 and the soft deadline passed, so Arch made the last three annotations directly and the iteration closed partial with the confirmation outstanding.",
        "minutes_lost": 12
      },
      {
        "category": "suite_insensitive_to_field_change",
        "summary": "Both full-suite runs returned an identical 113 passed / 3 skipped under either setting of the flag, so the registered tests could not detect a change that moves hbl agreement on a real capture from 33.9 m to 3.09 m. Pass/fail was uninformative and only the field-level A/B decided the issue.",
        "evidence": "devel-loop/loop_state/1dmix057-baseline-full-suite.txt and 1dmix057-flipped-full-suite.txt both end in 113 passed, 3 skipped. The field-level comparison in 1dmix057-wscale-capture-threeway.txt shows global_oce_latlon hbl max_abs 3.390e+01 to 3.092e+00 and cells above 1 percent 146/11575 to 10/11575 across the same two configurations. The same measurement also exposed a ghat disagreement of 394/394 active cells that the existing passing test likewise cannot detect, now filed as 1DMIX-058.",
        "minutes_lost": 0
      }
    ],
    "solutions": [
      {
        "problem": 0,
        "action": "filed",
        "issue": "TEAM-DOC-SWEEP-001",
        "reason": "Needs a repeatable pre-brief sweep procedure rather than Arch recalling which documents mention a symbol; filed with the measured five-document spread so the procedure is justified by evidence rather than by this one bad experience."
      },
      {
        "problem": 1,
        "action": "filed",
        "issue": "TEAM-BUDGET-SIZING-001",
        "reason": "Recorded under the existing allocation-and-measurement owner because the actionable lesson is a sizing and instrument-choice one: a behaviour-changing default needs a field-level A/B budgeted from the start, not a suite run that cannot resolve the change."
      }
    ],
    "carry_forward": [
      "Before briefing a change to a named symbol or default, grep the whole repository for it and list every document that will need updating; a document discovered by a reviewer costs a correction round, and the allowance is two.",
      "A green suite does not establish that a behaviour change is harmless when its tolerances are wider than the change: measure the affected fields directly and treat pass/fail as a floor, not as the evidence."
    ],
    "no_problem_reason": ""
  },
